{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Interpreted the corrected eligibility matrix. All 13 events were read from the retained receipt: duplicate member, duplicate address, witness role changes, re-adding a removed identity and removing the sole remaining address were rejected, while add, promotion with the same address, witness add and two removals were accepted. The last event is the concern: a RemoveNode for an identity not in the address set was accepted, records that identity as Removed and thereby blocks any later AddNode for it, which, if it also holds in a realistic configuration, would let an operator typo permanently burn a node identity while removing nothing. Because that case used a membership object without the local node, the account is recorded as unresolved with defect_claim unresolved and the validity limit stated, rather than asserting a defect.\"}"}}
